    not_duplicate_of: []  # 8c6b
    pr_ref:  # 8c6b
    description: "Phase 6 recall, INV-mumov's L3 half (INV-linub's class in python), candidate 3 after the QuerySet chain (PR 1, measurement 0013) and the reverse-relation manager (PR 3, 0015). Pre-registered design + measurement: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/mumov_instwrite_09072026/PLAN.md.\n\nTHE PREMISE, measured at tip (dev 946ad85633) on a fixture through production analyze_python with two controls in the same run (fx/ + dump.py):\n  self.delete() in a DIRECT models.Model subclass  -> django.db.models:delete   CONTROL, WI-sozoj works\n  super().save() inside Order.save                 -> external:save             LOST\n  d.delete()  where d = Direct.objects.create(...) -> external:delete           LOST\n  p.save()    where p = Payment()                  -> external:save             LOST (receiver_type_hint IS stamped; only the re-key is missing)\n  x.save() untyped param                           -> external:save             correct\n  f.save() on a local non-model class              -> resolves to the project method, correct\nAn instrument defect was found and corrected before any number was quoted: the first probe silently dropped every RESOLVED edge and would have reported four of these as \"no edge emitted\" -- the emission clause INV-mumov already has refuted.\n\nTHE FINDING THAT MAKES THIS THE SLICE (write_scan.py, pretix, 2,923 save/delete sites classified by how the receiver could be typed). Of the 306 sites whose receiver resolves to a model, 215 (70%) call a save the PROJECT OVERRIDES -- so the call correctly resolves to the project method and is not an I/O primitive at all. Independently: 56 of pretix's 66 save overrides and 20 of its 49 delete overrides call super().<m>(), and super().save() emits the `external` sentinel. On a real Django project the ORM write is therefore not usually at x.save(); it is at the super().save() inside the override, and that site is the CHOKEPOINT for every upstream call. A false NEGATIVE on a write primitive.\n\nWHAT SHIPS -- three rules, one mechanism (the model lineage):\n  R1 LINEAGE. The model gate becomes DjangoRelationIndex.model_ids (repo-wide, already transitive through resolved project bases) instead of _class_directly_extends_django_model's direct-dotted-base-only test; the direct test stays as the no-index fallback. pretix: 11 sites (self.save/self.delete in a transitive model class).\n  R2 SUPER. super().save() / super().delete() lexically inside a model class -> django.db.models, GATED on no project base in the lineage defining that method. pretix: 61 of 63 sites (the 2 refused are OrderPosition.save / CartPosition.save, whose base AbstractPosition defines save -- their write is typed at AbstractPosition's own super().save()).\n  R3 TYPED RECEIVER. X.save() / X.delete() where X is an instance of a class in model_ids -> django.db.models, on the UNRESOLVED branch only, so a project-defined method still wins. pretix: ~105 sites.\nAlso: DjangoRelationIndex.__bool__ must count model_ids, or a Django repo with models but no relation/manager declaration passes None and R1-R3 die.\n\nNOT IN THIS PR, each already filed and staying filed: the loop variable of a for over a QuerySet (WI-nibum, 55 of these sites), setUp fields (WI-zamud, 995), forward-FK fields into the Site-3 map (WI-lurob).\n\nREFUTATION CONDITIONS, written before the code: (RC1) a site typed django.db.models whose receiver is not a model instance at read-back -- the named risk is ModelForm.save() / Serializer.save(), which are NOT ORM writes; one such site removes R3. (RC2) a super().save() typed in a class whose project base defines save (double-counting one logical write). (RC3) survey-wide read-back of every framework_dispatch=django_orm save/delete edge, as 0015 did for the relation markers.\n\nMEASURED THROUGH THE TAINT PATH (INV-linub 2026-09-04), not io-boundaries chain counts: the 0003 marginal-precision delta on pretix with kserve as the zero-move control, every added and removed situation adjudicated under ADR-0046's two axes. POSITIVE CONTROL pre-registered from 0015's own read-back: five of that measurement's nine false positives were structural pairings whose real carrier is an untyped instance .save(); R3 types exactly those carriers, so they must change -- if none does, the mechanism story is wrong and the write-up says so. The PR carries awaits_bakeoff_validation."  # 8c6b
    fields: {}  # 8c6b
